# Global theme colors

Source of truth: `app/styles/theme.css` (loaded from `app/root.tsx` / `app/routes/app.tsx`).

When adding or editing pages, components, or CSS:

- Never introduce new hardcoded hex/rgb colors for UI chrome (backgrounds, text, borders, buttons, focus rings, status).
- Use `var(--wl-*)` tokens: primary, primary-variant, secondary, accent, background, surface, text, text-secondary, text-disabled, border, border-strong, success, warning, error, info, and `*-soft` / `chart-*` variants.
- Prefer `--wl-*` over legacy `--ca-*` / one-off locals; if a local alias is needed, define it as `var(--wl-…)`.
- Storefront assets: keep `--ws-*` API but default them from `--wl-*`.
- Palette changes: edit only `:root` in `app/styles/theme.css`.

See also `agent.md` → **Global theme**.
